# DDD Guidelines

## Strategic Design
- **Bounded context** — modules under `apps/api/src/modules/*` (chat, feed, comments, auth, …)
- **Context mapping** — integrate via application use cases, domain events, and ports — not cross-module repository calls

## Tactical Design
- **Entities** — identity (e.g. `Message`, `Conversation`, `Comment`)
- **Value objects** — immutable, compared by value (e.g. `MessageContent`)
- **Aggregates / aggregate root** — protect invariants; single entry point
- **Domain services** — rules that don’t belong on one entity
- **Repositories** — persistence abstraction only (`domain/repositories`, `infrastructure/prisma-*.repository.ts`)
- **Domain events** — past-tense facts (`chat.message_sent`, `comment.created`)

## Ubiquitous Language
Code names must match business language used in product (inbox, match, feed, conversation, …).

## Anti-patterns (forbidden)
- Anemic domain model with all logic in use cases
- Business logic in controllers or DTOs
- Fat repositories with business rules
- God services spanning unrelated contexts

## Domain Modeling Process
1. Identify actors → 2. Commands → 3. Events → 4. Invariants → 5. Aggregate boundaries
